<!--
  Corrected example: 4x ZED 2 stereo camera mount on a square mobile robot chassis.

  Verified against the actual zed_macro.urdf.xacro source (stereolabs/zed-ros2-wrapper,
  master branch). Real macro signature:
    params="name=zed model=zed enable_gnss=false custom_baseline=0 *gnss_origin"

  Key facts:
  - There is NO "parent" attribute on this macro. It only creates a standalone
    "${name}_camera_link" link; you must attach it to your robot yourself via
    a separate fixed joint.
  - The "*gnss_origin" block parameter has no default, so xacro requires a
    block to be passed even when enable_gnss=false (it's simply unused then).
-->
