<!--
  Notes:
  1. Each zed_camera call creates "<name>_camera_link", "<name>_camera_center",
     "<name>_left_camera_frame", "<name>_right_camera_frame", and their
     optical frames, all internally relative to "<name>_camera_link".
     Your external joint below each macro call is what actually positions
     that whole camera assembly on your chassis.

  2. The nested <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/> inside each <xacro:zed_camera>
     block is a required placeholder for the "*gnss_origin" block parameter.
     It has no effect unless you also pass enable_gnss="true".

  3. Overlap math unchanged: ZED2 FOV (~110 deg) - 90 deg spacing between
     adjacent camera axes = ~20 deg overlap per seam on a square chassis.

  4. If your local zed_wrapper install differs from this master-branch source
     (e.g., older tagged release), re-verify with:
       grep -n 'xacro:macro name="zed_camera"' \
         $(ros2 pkg prefix zed_wrapper)/share/zed_wrapper/urdf/zed_macro.urdf.xacro
-->
